# Paymob

Reuse `src/lib/paymob.ts`. Do not invent HMAC field order or a custom card form. For API shapes and HMAC concat, read `.agents/skills/paymob-integration/references/` (official skill) before guessing.

- Intention: `POST https://accept.paymob.com/v1/intention/` with `Authorization: Token <PAYMOB_SECRET_KEY>`
- Amounts: integer piastres. `sum(items.amount * quantity) === amount`
- `billing_data` via `buildBillingData()` (unused fields `"NA"`)
- Checkout: `unifiedCheckoutUrl(clientSecret)` — new Intention every attempt (`client_secret` is single-use)
- `special_reference` = `{token}:{kind}:{attemptId}` where `kind` is `deposit` | `balance`. Also `extras: { token, kind, attemptId }`
- Checkout `kind=deposit` only from `awaiting_deposit`; `kind=balance` only from `awaiting_balance`. Amount from server price, never the body.

Webhook (`/api/paymob/webhook`): verify HMAC with `verifyTransactionHmac` **before** any UPDATE. Ignore `type !== "TRANSACTION"`. Match `obj.order.merchant_order_id`. Use `isPaid()`. Never mark paid on HMAC mismatch (401) and never skip verify — fallback is `POST /api/paymob/inquiry` (Transaction Inquiry by `merchant_order_id`), not trusting the redirect.

Official skill: `.cursor/skills/paymob-integration`.

Register the same webhook URL on card **and** wallet integrations in the Paymob dashboard. After redirect, the client polls `/o/[token]`; query params are not proof of payment.

Official Paymob MCP (`https://mcp.paymob.com/mcp`, project `.cursor/mcp.json`) is for live account ops (test intentions, list transactions, balances). It does **not** replace HMAC. Do not write `*_paid_at` or flip status from MCP output. Confirm with the user before any write; use `is_live: false` until they say otherwise. Never put API keys in mcp.json.
